<main>
  <section id="about"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <div class="about" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
      <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Keneisha Sanap">
      <div>
        <p class="lead">I connect brands with the creators, partners, and audiences that make them matter.</p>
        <p>I've built marketing from zero twice: growing a nonprofit's social presence into the foundation for a platform that now reaches 1M+ views, and launching a university partnerships program that brought on Red Bull and Good Molecules. With a background in live broadcast and certifications in influencer marketing and media relations, I can pitch the idea, brief the creator, and tell the story. I also work AI-fluent: I use generative AI to speed up research and ideation, then pressure-test what it gives me against real consumer insight.</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b>1M+</b><span>views on a platform I helped build</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>800K+</b><span>live newscast viewers</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>200+</b><span>guests per activation</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b>4</b><span>industry certifications</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn solid" href="#" data-resume>View resume</a>
          <a class="btn" href="mailto:keneisha.sanap.work@gmail.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Email me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section id="experience"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <p class="lede">Graduating Magna Cum Laude in December 2026 and available full-time from January 2027.</p>
    <div id="exp"></div>
  </div></section>

  <section id="abroad"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Study abroad</h2>
    <div class="abroad">
      <div>
        <h3>Honors Cohort, Europe</h3>
        <p class="sub">Vienna, Florence, Budapest, Prague, and Germany</p>
        <p class="de">Ich spreche etwas Deutsch.<span>I speak a little German.</span></p>
        <p>Backpacking across Europe, striking up conversations with strangers on the EuroRail, and talking to locals in my best attempt at German taught me that stories are deeply relational. At the core of my learning was one question: how can I tell a story with the tools I have?</p>

      </div>
